  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 AM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nToday will continue to be hot, with heat index values nearing 113 \nover Jim Wells, Kleberg, Nueces, and San Patricio counties this \nafternoon. A Heat Advisory is in effect this afternoon. \n\nDeep moisture will continue to stream into the area from multiple \nsources over the next few days. Increased low level flow will herald \nin Gulf moisture, while an upper level low will bring in deep \nmoisture from the Pacific as well as the remnants of Hurricane Polo. \nPWATs will increase to nearly 2.5 inches today and Thursday, with \nsome guidance hinting at PWATs nearing 2.7 inches (though this seems \nexcessive). As shortwaves embedded in the trough move toward the \narea, a 20-35% of showers and thunderstorms will develop today. By \nThursday, widespread convection is expected to develop across the \narea as a pre-frontal surface trough develops. \n\nA cold front is then expected to move across the area Friday, \ncontinuing our heavy rain chances through the weekend. Guidance has \ncome into a little better agreement, indicating the cold front \nstalling Friday night along the coast, then pushing off the coast \nSunday. Confidence is still low to medium regarding the timing, \nstrength, and if and where the cold front will stall. Regardless, \nmedium rain chances will continue through the weekend as the upper \nlow moves slowly east across Texas.",
